+
+## Webhooks
+
+- The form's "Webhook URL" field is `bot[webhook_url]`. Leaving the key out of a request leaves the
+  webhook as it is; an empty value removes it.
+- `messages#create` (the composer only, not the bot API, so bots answering bots can't loop) calls
+  `messages::bot_webhooks::deliver_later` after the broadcast. Everything else happens in a job on
+  the `JobKind::BotWebhook` queue (`Jobs::perform_later_on`), which has its own workers, so neither
+  the poster nor other jobs wait on a slow bot.
+- The job reads `message.mentionees` (room members), drops the author, and keeps the active bots
+  with a webhook (`Webhook::of_active_bots`). Each bot gets its own payload, posted concurrently:
+
+  ```json
+  { "event": "mention",
+    "author":  { "id": 7, "name": "Alice" },
+    "room":    { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/<bot key>/messages" },
+    "message": { "id": 118, "body": { "text": "…", "html": "<stored rich text>" }, "link": "/rooms/5/@118" } }
+  ```
+
+  `text` is `plain_text_body` with every `@<bot name>` removed, then stripped (as Rails Campfire's
+  `without_recipient_mentions`). `room.name` is the display name for the bot (direct rooms have
+  none of their own). Paths are relative.
+- `integrations::webhooks::deliver` does the HTTP: no proxy, no private network guard (bots often
+  run on `localhost` or the LAN; the push and unfurl clients keep theirs), 7 s connect and read
+  timeouts, 15 s for the whole exchange, answers up to 1 MB.
+- Answers: `200` with `text/plain` (escaped, lines joined with `<br>`) or `text/html` (stored as rich
+  text, sanitized on render) is created as the bot's message, if it's still in the room, and
+  broadcast and pushed like any. `204`, other 2xx, other types or a blank body post nothing.
+  Failures (other statuses, timeouts, connection errors) are only logged.
+- Broadcasting outside a request uses `messages::broadcast_create_at` with the base URL and host
+  captured from the posting request.
+- Bots are `users` rows in the room, so the mention autocomplete (`autocompletable/users`) already
+  suggests them.
